# Model weights: never commit these, they are hundreds of gigabytes.
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.bin

# Server logs and runtime state.
*.log
llm-state.json
instances/

# Build artifacts.
build-win/
*.zip
*.exe
*.dll

# Script backups. These hold PREVIOUS versions of the control script, which may
# still contain the addresses and API key this repository was scrubbed of.
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.ubak
*.orig

# Benchmark inputs and test fixtures. Vision testing is often done on real
# documents; never let one reach a public repository.
bench-prompt.json
*-test.png
*-test.jpg
test-images/

# Question sets, and this one is not about privacy.
#
# A published question set stops measuring. It is absorbed into the next
# generation of training data, and a model that has read the answers scores
# high without knowing anything. That is not a hypothesis: the public multiple
# choice benchmark rates two of the models measured here at 88 percent and
# cannot tell them apart, while a set nobody outside this house has seen puts
# them at 73 and 68 and separates them.
#
# So the scripts, the method and the numbers are published, and the questions
# never are. Anyone can rebuild a set from the schema in docs; nobody can train
# on ours.
bench/epreuves.jsonl
bench/inedit/
*.jsonl

# Local secrets.
.env
.env.*
api-key.txt
*.key
*.pem
